; Stage 15 B3′ — defect #4, pinned. Before B3′ `strip-ns-qualifier` threw away a
; type spelling's qualifier and looked the bare name up in a flat registry, so
; ANY qualifier resolved — including one naming a namespace that does not exist
; anywhere in the compilation unit:
;
;   (defn f2 ((x (ref zzz/Fox))):i32 (return (x n)))   ; compiled, linked, ran
;
; The qualifier is now resolved through this file's import environment like every
; other name, so an unbound one resolves to nothing. `Cat` is defined right here,
; which is the sharp version of the test: the type exists, the bare spelling
; works, and only the bogus qualifier is refused.
(defstruct Cat n:i32)

(defn b3-take ((c (ref nope/Cat))):i32 (return (_get c n)))

(defn main ():i32 (return 0))
